  "scope": "# Review \u2014 8291f3ee7e54\nAssignment `review-e1b6d098e7e50811`; candidate generator `3.1.0`, SHA-256 `5e1e28490be83e36d8e8243e23082015d5110e9ed98a3a189941476443fcb2af`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: generated lessons made largest-component selection indistinguishable from a union-bbox shortcut; a controlled detached same-color singleton branch now falsifies that rival.\nThe canonical rule is unchanged: hash `d9bb03e0e2ec`, rule-text SHA-256 `30a8c3d1be93295f9c2636c0542381e8943aa10495e71124d7d95250ec2860fc`.\nFocused production checks cover canonical profiles, generalized boundaries, one accepted distractor, two rejected same-color distractors, and forced 12\u00d712/3-layer plus 22\u00d722/5-layer distractor generation.\nExact canonical Racket evidence covers four inputs; all pass generator-domain checks, and the union-bbox rival is refuted by the hand witness and both generated boundary cases.\nA separate proposed/unapproved `ring_order` prototype preserves the exact canonical default and adds `smallest_outside`; it does not modify production or canonical authority.\nParametric evidence retains both fixed settings with 2 demonstrations + 4 distinct queries each, 12 exact Racket labels total, and zero ambiguities against the sole declared alternate.\nPublic task `45a5af55` supplied only the order-to-ring-depth idea; lineage and inherited difficulty are explicitly unverified.\nBoth bounded supplementary tickets are complete; one recommends a cost-aware allocation pilot, and one finds a peer prototype privacy-safe but limited to a single retained query.\nAssessment: needs maintainer attention for source approval and variant review; no approval or training-admission change is claimed.\nScope limit: no full production battery, peer battery, model job, or corpus-wide census was run; changed-scope verification only.",
